## Title: Furniture Finder
## Author: @Aldimar77
## Version: 0.1.0
## AddOnVersion: 1
## APIVersion: 101050
## OptionalDependsOn: LibCharacterKnowledge
## Description: Adds source, item ID, quality, and collection info to furnishing tooltips (inventory, bank, and Housing Editor). UI-only, console-safe: no external network calls, no gameplay changes.
## SavedVariables: FurnitureFinder_SavedVars FurnitureFinderOwnershipData
## IsLibrary: false

FurnitureFinder_ExportData.lua
FurnitureFinder_ExportAPI.lua
FurnitureFinder_Ownership.lua
FurnitureFinder.lua

; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; NOTE:
;
; 1) APIVersion above (101050) is CONFIRMED against the live client via
;    GetAPIVersion(), checked in-game on 2026-08-25. (Wookiefriseur's PTS
;    dump reported 101051, one ahead of live at the time -- expected,
;    since PTS usually runs slightly ahead of live.)
;
; 2) Console submission goes through the official Developer Uploader Tool
;    (help.elderscrollsonline.com -> "ESO Console Add-ons - Developer
;    Uploader Tool"). Console builds are UI-only and get reviewed before
;    they appear in the in-game browse menu -- this file as written already
;    respects that (no LibHttp-style network access exists in ESO's Lua
;    sandbox on any platform, so there's nothing to strip out).
;
; 3) 2026-08-28: replaced FurnitureFinderData.lua (our own hand-converted,
;    category-label-only data) with Wookiefriseur's real export + accessor
;    files (FurnitureFinder_ExportData.lua / FurnitureFinder_ExportAPI.lua).
;    These are their _rendered.lua and _api.lua verbatim, with one line
;    each changed: the original top-level "return ..." was replaced with
;    a global assignment, since ESO's addon loader discards top-level
;    return values from manifest-declared files (there's no loadfile/
;    require capturing it the way their standalone example.lua uses).
;    Verified the adapted files behave identically to the original
;    loadfile pattern via a real Lua interpreter before this went in-game.
;    This gives real vendor/location/price/achievement detail instead of
;    just a category label.
; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
